The write tool errored because the entity_ref is empty `{}`. It seems my JSON object parameters are coming through as empty `{}` when there might be parsing issues. Let me try string values instead, because looking at the description for `entity_ref`, it says examples like:

`{"kind": "response", "id": "resp-1"}` etc.

But maybe using a string like `"request:token_req"` would also work?

Looking at the schema again:
```
{
  "entity_ref": {
    "description": "typed handle, shape `{kind, id, parent?}`. Examples:\n`{\"kind\": \"response\", \"id\": \"resp-1\"}`,\n`{\"kind\": \"spec\", \"id\": \"openapi.yaml\"}`,\n`{\"kind\": \"variable\", \"id\": \"access_token\"}`.",
    "anyOf": [{"type": "object", "additionalProperties": {}}, {"type": "string"}],
  }
}
```

So entity_ref can be either object OR string. Let me try the string version.

